.TH XSAKURA 1 "October 2026" "xsakura 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xsakura \- grow a cherry blossom tree in your terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xsakura
[\fIcolor\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xsakura
draws a sakura tree with half-block pixel art. The tree grows from a sprout,
sprouts bare branches, bursts into bloom and then sheds petals that drift in
the wind. The tree grows from the bottom edge of the terminal and nothing else
is drawn, so the background stays transparent and it fits nicely on top of a
wallpaper. It needs a terminal with 24-bit color
(256 colors work as a fallback) and a font with the half block characters.
.SH COLORS
Give a color as a single-dash option, for example
.BR "xsakura \-red" .
.TP
.B \-sakura
Soft cherry blossom pink (default).
.TP
.B \-pink \-red \-orange \-yellow \-gold \-green \-cyan \-blue \-purple \-magenta \-white
Single colored trees.
.TP
.B \-rainbow
Every blossom cluster gets its own color.
.TP
.BI \-hex " RRGGBB"
Any custom color.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-seed " \fIN\fR"
Reproducible tree. The same seed and window size give the same tree.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-print
Print the finished tree to standard output and exit. Handy for screenshots
and for a shell greeting. This is also the default when output is not a terminal.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-instant
Skip the growing animation.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-time " \fISEC\fR"
Quit after SEC seconds.
.TP
.BI \-\-cycle " SEC"
Grow a brand new tree SEC seconds after the previous one finished.
.TP
.BI \-\-speed " X"
Animation speed multiplier (default 1.0).
.TP
.BI \-\-grow " SEC"
Seconds the tree needs to grow (default 9).
.TP
.BI \-\-petals " N"
Number of falling petals. The default scales with the window width.
.TP
.BI \-\-wind " X"
Wind strength. Negative values blow to the left (default 1.0).
.TP
.BI \-\-scale " X"
Tree size multiplier (default 1.0). The tree always shrinks to fit the window.
.TP
.BI \-\-width " N" ", " \-\-height " N"
Size in terminal cells (default: size of the terminal).
.TP
.BI \-\-fps " N"
Frames per second (default 30).
.TP
.BR \-\-truecolor ", " \-\-256
Force the color mode. By default it is detected from COLORTERM and TERM.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List the available colors.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help ", " \-v ", " \-\-version
Show help or the version.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B q, Esc, Ctrl\-C
Quit.
.TP
.B r
Grow a new tree.
.TP
.B space
Pause or resume.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
xsakura                        # the classic
xsakura \-green                # a green tree
xsakura \-hex ff8800 \-i         # an orange tree, already grown
xsakura \-p \-s 7                # print a finished tree for a screenshot
xsakura \-\-cycle 20             # screensaver: new tree every 20 seconds
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
Written for people who like pretty terminals.
